      "content": "<columns>\nAmerica a Prophecy is a 1793 prophetic book by the English poet and illustrator [https://coda.io/d/_d0SvdI3KSto/_suhVOaG1](https://coda.io/d/_d0SvdI3KSto/_suhVOaG1).\n\n[https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/America_a_Prophecy](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/America_a_Prophecy) \n\n[https://coda.io/d/_d0SvdI3KSto/_suRfidAo](https://coda.io/d/_d0SvdI3KSto/_suRfidAo) \n\n|||\n\n[https://www.youtube.com/live/5O5myx5XkBc](https://www.youtube.com/live/5O5myx5XkBc)\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/live/5O5myx5XkBc\n\n|||\n\n\n</columns>\n\n  - The Doors of Perception are the Threshold of Prediction: Active Inference and William Blake's Theory of Seeing [https://zenodo.org/records/18600041](https://zenodo.org/records/18600041) \n\n  - [https://zenodo.org/records/18807971](https://zenodo.org/records/18807971) Before Pragmatism Had a Name: Blake's \"America A Prophecy\" Anticipates American Anticipatory Epistemology\n\n",
